    // The three below come from the game itself rather than from a donor title: a GSC script run
    // in Cold War asked the engine for these by name across 233 weapons, and the offset holding
    // the matching value for every one of them is the field. No weapon disagrees, which is a
    // stronger claim than any cross-title inference in this file - the engine named the value.
    //
    // Times are whole milliseconds here, so 0.092s reads as 92 and 2.4s as 2400. That is the
    // "times": "milliseconds" rule in porting.jsonc, not a special case for these fields.
    //
    // burstCount is the one nothing else could have placed: it has zero references anywhere in
    // Cold War's own scripts, so whether the engine even exposed it was unknowable without
    // asking. It does, and it reads 3 on exactly the three-round-burst weapons.
    {"offset": "0xf44", "name": "firetime", "source": "engine", "kind": "int", "form": "int", "observed": 501, "agreed": 233, "examples": []},

