    // ---- named from the engine's own weapon field table ----
    // The engine resolves weapon.<field> by hashing the name and looking it up in a table of
    // (nameHash, type, offset, size, pool). That table is the complete list of what the engine
    // exposes - 428 fields - so none of these is inferred from a donor title or matched by value.
    // The engine states the offset. See the weapon-field-table note for how it is read.
    //
    // Only fields the table gives a plain offset for are here. A hundred of the 428 are computed
    // by a getter and have no single offset - firetime and clipsize among them - and those still
    // have to be found by matching values. Fields sharing one offset are left out too: five
    // weapon-class tests all read tunables 0x5ac and would otherwise be five identical wrong ints.
    //
    // The flags are one byte each and packed, so most of their offsets are not four-aligned. They
    // read with "form": "byte"; reading one as an int would take three neighbours with it.

    {"offset": "0x20", "name": "spawninfluencer", "source": "engine", "kind": "string", "form": "string", "observed": 534, "examples": []},
    {"offset": "0x238", "name": "hackertriggerorigintag", "source": "engine", "kind": "string", "form": "string", "observed": 0, "examples": []},
