    // ---- computed fields, found by matching values ----
    // The engine's field table names these but gives them no offset: a getter serves them, so
    // there is nothing in the table to read. Each was found the other way round - the game was
    // asked for it by name across 233 weapons, and this is the offset carrying the matching value
    // for every one of them.
    //
    // meleetime and meleechargetime are state timers, the length the animation is played over.
    // The note in this project said the engine does not report such things; asking for all 36 of
    // them by name got 5 back, so it reports some and not others. drop, raise and the ads
    // transitions really are absent - that part was right.

    {"offset": "0xe94", "name": "fusetime", "source": "engine", "kind": "int", "form": "int", "observed": 142, "agreed": 233, "examples": []},

    // NOT A REAL NAME. The game does not call this field anything - this label was made up here to describe what the field was seen to hold. It is a guess at the meaning, not the game's own word, and it may be wrong. Names without this comment are the game's own.
    {"offset": "0xeec", "name": "adsTransInTime", "source": "observed", "kind": "int", "form": "int", "observed": 0, "examples": []},

