    {"offset": "0x1074", "name": "lockonspeed", "source": "engine", "kind": "int", "form": "int", "observed": 53, "agreed": 233, "examples": []},

    // Milliseconds, and the length of the weapon's own inspect animation: across 198 weapons the value is that animation's length to within one percent on half of them and the median ratio is 0.999, over 55 distinct lengths against 56 distinct values. Found by using animation length as the oracle - the same sweep rediscovers reloadtime at 0x1028, which is how it is known to work.
    // NOT A REAL NAME. The game does not call this field anything - this label was made up here to describe what the field was seen to hold. It is a guess at the meaning, not the game's own word, and it may be wrong. Names without this comment are the game's own.
    {"offset": "0x1090", "name": "inspecttime", "source": "observed", "kind": "int", "form": "int", "observed": 533, "examples": []},
